Functions implementing internal features. Not all of these function pointers must be defined for a given type. The required members are nonzero, copyswap, copyswapn, setitem, getitem, and cast. These are assumed to be non- NULL and NULL entries will cause a program crash. The other functions may be NULL which will just mean reduced functionality for that data-type. (Also, the nonzero function will be filled in with a default function if it is NULL when you register a user-defined data-type). typedef struct {
