 The C file is given below. The ufunc generated takes two arguments A and B. It returns a tuple whose first element is A*B and whose second element is logit(A*B). Note that it automatically supports broadcasting, as well as all other properties of a ufunc. #define PY_SSIZE_T_CLEAN
#include <Python.h>
#include "numpy/ndarraytypes.h"
#include "numpy/ufuncobject.h"
#include "numpy/halffloat.h"
#include <math.h>

/*
 * multi_arg_logit.c
 * This is the C code for creating your own
 * NumPy ufunc for a multiple argument, multiple
 * return value ufunc. The places where the
 * ufunc computation is carried out are marked
 * with comments.
 *
 * Details explaining the Python-C API can be found under
 * 'Extending and Embedding' and 'Python/C API' at
 * docs.python.org .
